# Edge-function deploy manifest — source of truth for `scripts/deploy-edge-function.sh`.
#
# Format: name|verify_jwt   (one row per deployable function; '#' lines and blanks ignored)
#
# verify_jwt mirrors the LIVE prod config as of 2026-06-25,
# read from the Supabase management API — NOT inferred from the function's auth code. This
# is deliberate: a re-deploy must preserve current gateway behavior exactly. `false` means
# the function self-authenticates (or is service-invoked) and is deployed with
# `--no-verify-jwt`; `true` means the gateway enforces the JWT and the function is deployed
# plain. Regenerate with: supabase functions list (or the management API) and copy verify_jwt.
#
# Every directory under supabase/functions/ (except _shared) MUST appear here exactly once,
# and every row MUST have a matching directory — the deploy script refuses on any drift, so a
# newly added function cannot ship until its flag is recorded here.
ai-proxy|false
sms-webhook|false
post-purchase-confirm|false
upsert-profile|false
email-scheduler|false
verify-tables|false
weekly-summary|true
welcome-email|false
trial-day-3|false
trial-day-7|false
trial-day-12|false
trial-day-13|false
rc-winback-webhook|false
extend-trial|true
delete-account|true
export-account|true
sms-opt-in|true
send-sms-broadcast|true
weekly-broadcast|true
weekly-summary-scheduler|true
sms-daily-quotes|true
